WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.289
Establish visual hierarchy.

00:00:01.289 --> 00:00:04.296
Decide what the reader should notice first.

00:00:04.296 --> 00:00:09.450
Use size, weight, and spacing to guide the eye through a screen.

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:12.887
Name the user task in a clear heading.

00:00:12.887 --> 00:00:15.464
Group related details beneath the heading.

00:00:15.464 --> 00:00:18.471
Give the next action a distinct treatment.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.383
Organize a form.

00:00:20.383 --> 00:00:25.915
A good form lets the user understand, complete, and correct each field.

00:00:25.915 --> 00:00:28.681
Keep its label visible throughout editing.

00:00:28.681 --> 00:00:31.907
Name the requested value above its input.

00:00:31.907 --> 00:00:35.134
Place a short example beside the field.

00:00:35.134 --> 00:00:38.361
Explain how to repair an invalid value.

00:00:38.917 --> 00:00:41.010
Plan a responsive layout.

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:44.675
Choose a reading order before arranging columns.

00:00:44.675 --> 00:00:49.909
As space shrinks, preserve the relationship between context and action.

00:00:49.909 --> 00:00:52.526
Show reading content beside navigation.

00:00:52.526 --> 00:00:55.667
Move navigation behind a labelled control.

00:00:55.667 --> 00:00:58.808
Test reading order and keyboard focus.

